<title>GERMANY: W. German Dec industrial orders fall 1.4 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>W. German Dec industrial orders fall 1.4 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS     Dec 96     Nov 96     Dec 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   -1.4	 -0.8	 +0.3</p>
<p> Year-on-year			+2.7	 +4.5	  n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		 95.3	 96.7	 92.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted, provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details (mth-on-mth)</p>
<p>				   Dec 96   Nov 96   Dec 96 index</p>
<p> Intermediate goods	   +1.4	-1.2     100.5</p>
<p> Capital goods		  -7.0	+1.1	92.6</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables   +1.9	-3.2	87.5</p>
<p> Domestic orders		-0.6	unch	87.4</p>
<p> Foreign orders		 -2.7	-1.8     111.1</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Nov/Dec 96 with Sept/Oct 96:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		    unch</p>
<p>Two month comparison Nov/Dec 96 with Nov/Dec 95:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		    +0.8</p>
<p> Domestic orders			-2.1</p>
<p> Foreign orders			 +5.5</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		   +4.2</p>
<p> Capital goods			  -1.6</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	   -3.5</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
